{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa","text":"Vertices","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A wrapper that adds a rule, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", can own any mutable directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation as its base through this protocol and work on it without extra hashing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each vertex has a key: its index in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertices.Index == Int"},{"type":"text","text":"). On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedPseudograph"},{"type":"text","text":") the key is the vertex’s slot, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":". On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" it is the vertex’s position, which never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes while the vertex exists and may leave holes. The underscored members read and write the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph by key, so a wrapper hashes a vertex once and then works on keys."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"’s laws:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_key(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_vertex(atKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is its inverse."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a vertex with key "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equal the unprefixed members for that vertex."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the far ends’ keys, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_sourceKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_targetKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the endpoints’ keys."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_insertVertex(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices.endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" inserts the edge and returns its position. On a simple graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":"), an edge already present is not inserted again and its position is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_removeVertex(atKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes the vertex and every edge at it. If the representation fills","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the hole by moving another vertex in (a swap-remove), it returns that vertex’s old key, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that vertex’s key becomes ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Otherwise it returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and no other key changes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeEdge(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the edge at a live position and returns it, and traps on any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position. Removing an edge changes no key."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeVertex(atKey: _key(of: v)!)"},{"type":"text","text":", returning the removed instance."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_built(vertices:sourceKeys:targetKeys:reportingPositions:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"type":"text","text":", then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for each vertex in order, then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for each pair"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in order. It gives the same graph and the same position for each pair."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A wrapper may keep one table entry per 1024 keys, from the smallest live key to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"vertices.endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", plus O(1) per live vertex. That matches the representation’s own page"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"table. On a dense representation the keys are "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". On "},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"span can exceed the vertex count, because removals leave holes and a decoded graph may start at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any position. Its decoder bounds the span at "},{"code":"16 × vertexCount + 64","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pages. Keys before the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smallest live key cost nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_successorKeys(ofKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" return the stored rows typed as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SuccessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"PredecessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whose elements here are keys. On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation keys and indices coincide. On "},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the elements are positions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which are vertex indices only while the graph has no holes. "},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then unavailable, but the key rows are not."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"insert(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not a requirement because its return type varies by representation."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns "},{"code":"(inserted:memberAfterInsert:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the multigraphs return the new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position, and a wrapper that rejects edges returns an optional. Generic code inserts an edge by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key with "},{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The underscored members are for wrappers inside the library. Callers use the representations’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove"},{"text":" members, which take vertices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"MutableDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph.swift#L54"},"roleHeading":"Protocol","title":"MutableDirectedGraph","symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015MutableDirectedA0P","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"],"type":"inheritsFrom"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/insert(_:)":{"kind":"symbol","required":true,"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"insert"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> (inserted"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":", memberAfterInsert"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"insert(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Inserts ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with no edges, if it is not already a vertex.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/insert(_:)"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertices-swift.associatedtype":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","title":"Vertices","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertices-swift.associatedtype","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","required":true,"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertices"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Collection","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/init()":{"kind":"symbol","required":true,"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"title":"init()","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The empty graph."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/init()"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","title":"MutableDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/removealledges(keepingcapacity:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"removeAllEdges"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"keepingCapacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","role":"symbol","title":"removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Removes every edge, keeping every vertex and its key.","type":"text"}],"required":true},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"DirectedGraph","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods. In-adjacency usually costs extra"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage, so representations that store only out-adjacency conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" alone."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remove(_:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/remove(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"remove","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","role":"symbol","title":"remove(_:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Removes ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and every edge at it.","type":"text"}],"required":true},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Removes every vertex and edge.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/removeall(keepingcapacity:)","title":"removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"removeAll","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"keepingCapacity","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"required":true,"type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)":{"required":true,"abstract":[{"text":"Reserves space for at least ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" vertices and ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" edges.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/reservecapacity(vertexcount:edgecount:)","title":"reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reserveCapacity"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"vertexCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"edgeCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remove(edge:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Removes one copy of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge"},{"text":". On a representation with parallel edges it removes the newest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copy. Never inserts or removes a vertex.","type":"text"}],"title":"remove(edge:)","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/remove(edge:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"remove"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"edge"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedEdge","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedEdgeV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedEdgeV","text":"DirectedEdge","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Verte